{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1785087894,"nonce":"y5sfy4shCFkPqEIhKnqfhXWmVT0=","title":"The `version` step of `.scarab/dogfood.yaml` settles as `failed` with failure","message":"class **`Step`** — the verdict meaning \"the command ran and exited non-zero\" —\nwhile **no Pod is ever created for it**. Reproducible across three consecutive\nruns on the local-helm colima stack.\n\n\nRuns `019f9ef2-2785-7681-9cf8-e4df84af3ede` and\n`019f9f2b-10b0-7661-980e-c238be313823` (both at `.scarab/dogfood.yaml` as of\ncommit a45d77a):\n\n- `GET /v1/runs/{id}` → `version: failed`, `attempt_list: [{id: a1, failure:\n  \"step\", outcome: \"failed\"}]`, `attempts: 1`.\n- `kubectl get pods -n scarab -l scarab.io/run=\u003cid\u003e` lists the checkout, lint and\n  every test-leg Pod — and **no `version` Pod at all**. Other steps' Pods carry\n  that label reliably, so this is absence, not a selector problem.\n- `GET /v1/runs/{id}/steps/version/logs` returns empty.\n- The server log shows `log tail: step Pod not ready yet, backing off` for lint\n  and all three test legs, and **nothing whatsoever for `version`** — the control\n  plane never even tried to tail it.\n- `POST /v1/runs/{id}/steps/version/retry` returns 202 but creates no Pod\n  (probably a no-op because the run is already terminal — that 202 is arguably\n  misleading in its own right).\n\n\nFailure class `Step` is a developer verdict: it asserts the author's command\nfailed. With no container ever started, that verdict cannot be true. Whatever the\nreal cause, it is being misreported as the author's fault — which is what made\nthis expensive to chase. An infra/config class would have pointed at the right\nplace immediately.\n\n\n`version` DID get a Pod and succeed in run `019f9ec6-5731-7f21-bce3-d6e4f82e6ed7`\n(Pod `scarab-version-a1-05d56a37`, Completed), at commit 52ee8fd. It broke between\nthat and a45d77a. What changed for the step in a45d77a: the command was rewritten\n(`mkdir -p /scarab/artifacts`, `$(git …)` capture, three `printf … \u003e\n/scarab/results/\u003cname\u003e.json` redirects) and **`artifacts: [\"*.txt\"]` was added**.\nNote `lint` also gained `artifacts:` in that commit and runs fine, so `artifacts:`\nalone is not sufficient to reproduce — the combination with results writes is the\nobvious thing to bisect.\n\n\nBlocks end-to-end verification of the results channel. The fix in PR #91 is\ncorrect against the sidecar's `*.json` glob but stays **unexercised**, and\n`deploy`'s `${{ outputs.version.* }}` assertions can never run while `version`\nfails.\n\n\nDispatch with server logging raised around the launch instant to see whether the\nPod spec is built at all, and bisect the a45d77a `version` changes (command\nrewrite vs `artifacts:`) one at a time.","files":null}]}